  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">support Member States with training, international cooperation and knowledge exc</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the only UN Agency with a mandate in earth sciences, and under its flagship International
Geoscience and Geoparks Programme (IGGP), UNESCO and its statutory partners the International
Union of Geological Sciences (IUGS) and the Global Geoparks Network (GGN) will continue to
foster capacity building, knowledge exchange and international research cooperation to promote
sustainable practices, help build resilience against geo-hazards, empower early career scientists in
the developing world and local communities in exploring, extracting and managing their natural
resources in an efficient, safe and sustainable manner. UNESCO Global Geoparks will be used to engage further in climate, biodiversity, DRR and other SDG related actions, including through dedicated educational programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
